Z||000005||JohnnyK||02-26-2001||12:49 PM||||Jodie Foster isn't accepting the role because she is afraid of failure. Clairisse is supposed to be different. She is supposed to have matured, etc. I have read that Foster wouldn't have been able to pull the acting off, and that Moore ( I think) did a far better job. I didn't find the movie gory at all, nor did I find it to be a slasher. The only part I'm a little iffy on is the brain part at the end (I don't know if it's possible?). I thought it was actually, as stimpy put it, "beautiful".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||02-26-2001||02:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>     Definitly not as good. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As Silence of the Lambs? No way! But it was a totally different movie. I don't consider it a sequel to SotL, but as it's own movie, and using "Silence" as expository dialogue, I think it is head and shoulders over any other horror movie in the past 10 years.||||reg||1
